    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The largest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/channel-islands">Channel Island</a>, it stayed with the English crown when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> lost Normandy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1204.</li><li>It keeps Norman customary law, its Royal Court and its own parliament, the States, as a Crown Dependency outside the UK.</li><li>Once a fortified frontier against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, it became a cod-trading, farming and later financial centre.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a> is named after the island: in 1664 the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york-maine">York</a> granted the land to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-carteret">Sir George Carteret</a>, a Jerseyman who had held the island for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-stuart">Stuarts</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

